28275	28362	28468	28468	he	121	" There is , perhaps , no class of men so cruelly misrepresented as the manufacturers of Great Britain ; surrounded on all sides by a population of labourers , crowded together exactly in proportion to the quantity of work the neighbouring factories are able to fur- nish — they are continually reproached both with giving too many hours of employment to their poor neighbours on the one hand , and with the poverty which is the inevitable lot of operatives with large families on the other .
